  => THE AXIS CANNOT SEE THIS SENSOR'S DEFECTS. Even its BEST measured
     floor sits 1.51 x above the largest excess the darks record, and on
     1 of 4 subjects examined no planted rung cleared at all. A PASS on
     this axis is silence, not a clean bill. Under the axis's own
     docstring rule those subjects are REFUSED, not PASS.

IS THE POWER RULE ACTUALLY ENFORCED?
  detector commissioned: prose-only -> False, subscript -> True, .get -> True
  dust.json records carrying a power arm : 0 of 26
  dust_verdict() ACCESSES a power field  : False
  ... mentions it only in prose          : True
  => the power rule is DISCLOSED IN PROSE AND ENFORCED NOWHERE. The axis
     docstring says a subject whose defects sit below the detection floor
     'is REFUSED rather than passed', but no record carries the arm and the
     verdict function never consults it. This is print-then-TEST: a value
     computed, published in a footnote, and conditioned on by nothing.
     dustaxis.main() calls run_subject(s) with commission defaulting to
     False, so the ladder that would have produced the arm never ran on the
     delivered path.

